  "classification": {
    "ELIMINATED": "the raw internal representation: each is a raw dereference of a tree node, a raw-pointer method call (dot-add / dot-cast) on the tree, a call to an internal tree-walk helper (sa_doall / sa_free_node / sa_free_leaf), or the trampoline transmute. The owned tree names the same node and slot by safe indexing, so the operation has no counterpart: its site id is gone from the census and no operation of its shape remains inside the subsystem.",
    "RELOCATED_TO_BOUNDARY": "an operation at the unavoidable boundary: it touches the opaque *mut OpenSslSa handle, the caller's leaf function pointer, or the crate allocator (CRYPTO_free, Box::from_raw). It survives, but only in a thin wrapper whose whole body is the boundary; the interior mechanism it used to interleave with is gone."
  },
