  "subsystem": {
    "files": [
      "src/runtime/sparse_array.rs"
    ],
    "id": "runtime/sparse-array",
    "mechanism": "the sixteen-way tree is a raw tree of *mut *mut c_void nodes reached by pointer arithmetic (p.add(i), (*p.add(i)).cast::<..>()), raw dereferences and a transmute trampoline. The reconstruction models it as an owned enum Node whose children are Boxes and whose deepest slots are the caller's values, and every descent, growth and walk is safe indexing/recursion on that value.",
    "why_internal": "OpenSslSa is pub(crate), #[no_mangle] nowhere, and exports no symbol: no public OpenSSL ABI symbol depends on its internals being raw. Its handle crosses into property/store.rs and rsa/ossl.rs only as an opaque *mut c_void, and no C reads its layout. The three observable fields (levels, top, nelem) and every entry-point signature are unchanged."
  },
  "tests": [
    "cargo test --lib",
    "cargo test --lib runtime::sparse_array"
  ]
}
